-- title:
--   Transport exponent shifts by 1+c under Frobenius re-basing
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, and a nonzero natural number $N$ with $r \nmid N$.
--
--   *Base rings.* Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$ irreducible, $\mathcal{O}$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, with residue ring $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ of cardinality $r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal{O}$; let $K_0$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$. Let `Onr` be a characteristic-zero domain which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism `Fr`, such that `Onr` is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of `Onr` satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo it (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over `Onr` of positive degree has a root modulo it (`hOnr_closed`), and `Fr` $x \equiv x^{r}$ modulo it for all $x$ (`hFr`). Throughout, `frobTwist Onr Fr k ψ` denotes $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{k}$ for $k \in \mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   *Quaternionic data.* Let $a, b \in \mathbb{Q}$ be such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a, b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`, i.e. $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and a finite place of $\mathbb{Q}$ is a division place of the algebra exactly when it lies over $r$ or over $\bar r$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order (`IsMaximalOrder`: an order, maximal among orders containing it) and contains every rational integer (`hΛℤ`). Let `coord` $: \Lambda \to \mathbb{W}(\mathbb{F}_{r^2})^{\,2}$ satisfy `IsOrderCoord Λ r coord`: it is additive, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, is multiplicative for the Frobenius-twisted product rule on pairs, is injective, has dense image in the $r$-adic sense, and matches reduced traces with $\mathbb{Z}_r$-traces of first coordinates.
--
--   *The reference object in characteristic $r$.* Let $A_0$ be a fake elliptic curve with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure over `Onr`$/(\pi)$, let $X_0$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module for $r$ over the same ring with `HasHeight 4`, and let $\theta_0$ be a system of two-variable formal coordinates for $A_0.f$ such that `A₀.IsFormalModuleVia coord X₀ θ₀` holds: $\theta_0$ is a formal coordinate system for the group law of $A_0$ with formal group $X_0.F$, and the $\Lambda$-action on points is given on coordinates by the series $\mathrm{act}((\mathrm{coord}\,m)_1) +_{X_0} \mathrm{act}((\mathrm{coord}\,m)_2)\circ \varpi$.
--
--   *The Drinfeld side.* Let $\iota : \mathbb{W}(\mathbb{F}_{r^2}) \to$ `Onr` be a ring homomorphism, and $\Phi$ a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over `Onr`$/(r)$ which is special for the reduction of $\iota$ and of height $4$. Let $M$ be a moduli package for $r$ over `Onr` which is a Zariski sheaf (`hM`), and let $\eta$ assign to each ring $B$ with a homomorphism $\psi :$ `Onr` $\to B$ in which $r$ is nilpotent a map from rigidified objects `Rigidified r Φ B` to $M.\mathrm{obj}\,B\,\psi$. The hypothesis `hη` has three clauses: for Noetherian $B$, two admissible rigidified objects have the same image under $\eta$ exactly when they are isomorphic in the sense of `Rigidified.IsIsomorphic`; $\eta$ is natural for ring homomorphisms over `Onr` applied to admissible objects; and every point of $M.\mathrm{obj}\,B\,\psi$ is, after passing to the members of a finite cover of $B$ by localisations at elements generating the unit ideal, the image under $\eta$ of an admissible rigidified object. Let $E_0$ be a ring homomorphism from the centralizer in the endomorphisms of $\Phi$ of the set $\mathrm{range}(\Phi.\mathrm{actEnd}) \cup \{\Phi.\mathrm{varpiEnd}\}$ to $M_2(K_0)$, and let `hE₀` assert that $E_0$ is injective and that for some $m$ every matrix over $\mathcal{O}$ becomes a value of $E_0$ after multiplication by $r^{m}$, and every value of $E_0$ becomes a matrix over $\mathcal{O}$ after multiplication by $r^{m}$.
--
--   *Comparison of the two residue rings and the reference isogeny.* Let $\kappa :$ `Onr`$/(\pi) \to$ `Onr`$/(r)$ be a ring homomorphism compatible with the two quotient maps (`hκ`), let $n_0 \in \mathbb{N}$ and let $\beta_0$ be a pair of power series over `Onr`$/(r)$ which is an isogeny of height $4 n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   *The period map $\Xi$ and its laws.* Let $\Xi$ assign to every Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with $\psi :$ `Onr` $\to_{\mathcal{O}} B$ and $\pi$ nilpotent in $B$ a map from rigidified curves `RigidifiedCurve r π A₀ B ψ` (pairs consisting of a fake elliptic curve over $B$ and a rigidification relative to $A_0$ and $\psi$) to $\mathcal{O}$-points `ModuliPackage.GPoint 𝒪 M B`. Four laws are assumed: `hΞleg`, that over a connected base (every idempotent is $0$ or $1$) the `Onr`-leg of $\Xi B \psi x$ is $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{k}$ for some $k \in \mathbb{Z}$; `hΞnat`, that $\Xi$ is compatible with base change along $\mathcal{O}$-algebra maps $\varphi : B \to B'$ when the curve and the rigidification are pulled back along $\varphi$; `hΞiso`, that $\Xi$ takes the same value on two rigidified curves over $(B,\psi)$ whenever their underlying curves are isomorphic compatibly with group law, $\Lambda$-action and level structure, and the rigidifications admit comparison maps $i_b$, $u_A$ and exponents $i_1, j_1$ making the displayed square commute after composing with multiplication by $r^{i_1}$, respectively $r^{j_1}$; and `hΞdef`, that over a connected Noetherian base in which $\pi$ and $r$ are nilpotent, for every rigidified curve $x$ and every formal module structure $(X,\theta)$ on its curve via `coord` there exist $j \le 1$ and $t :$ `Rigidified r Φ B` with $t.X = X$, with $t$ a rigidification transport of $x$ in the sense of `IsRigTransport θ₀ κ β₀` with parameter $j$, with $t$ admissible for $\iota$ and $\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$, and with $\Xi B \psi x$ equal to the point of `GPoint` with leg $\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$ and underlying moduli point $\eta$ applied to $t$.
--
--   *Frobenius and Verschiebung on the reference object.* Let $A_{0}^{r}$ be a second fake elliptic curve over `Onr`$/(\pi)$ together with $\mathrm{pr}_A : A_{0}^{r}.A \to A_0.A$ exhibiting $A_{0}^{r}$ as the pullback of $A_0$ along the residue map induced by `Fr` (`hprA`), and let $F : A_0.A \to A_{0}^{r}.A$ and $V : A_{0}^{r}.A \to A_0.A$ be morphisms over the base (`hF`, `hV`) which are homomorphisms for the group laws on points (`F_hom`, `V_hom`), commute with the $\Lambda$-action (`F_act`, `V_act`), preserve the property of factoring through the level structure (`F_lev`, `V_lev`), satisfy $P$ followed by $F$ followed by $V$ equals $r\cdot P$ and $Q$ followed by $V$ followed by $F$ equals $r \cdot Q$ on points (`V_F`, `F_V`), and are such that for every ring $C$ of characteristic $r$ and every point $x$ of $A_0.A$ with values in $C$, $x$ followed by $F$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_A$ equals $x$ precomposed with the $r$-power Frobenius of $C$ (`F_frob`).
--
--   *The base and the two rigidifications.* Let $B$ be a nontrivial Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with $\psi :$ `Onr` $\to_{\mathcal{O}} B$, with the image of $\pi$ nilpotent in $B$, and connected (every idempotent is $0$ or $1$). Let $E$ be a fake elliptic curve over $B$, let $\rho$ be a rigidification of $E$ relative to $A_0$ and $\psi$, and let $\rho^{+}$ be a rigidification of the same $E$ relative to $A_0$ and $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}$. The comparison data between them consists of: $u_b : \rho.E_b.A \to \rho^{+}.E_b.A$ with $u_b$ followed by $\rho^{+}.g_b$ equal to $\rho.g_b$ and $u_b$ followed by $\rho^{+}.E_b.f$ equal to $\rho.E_b.f$; a map $g_A' : \rho^{+}.A_b.A \to A_{0}^{r}.A$ exhibiting $\rho^{+}.A_b$ as the pullback of $A_{0}^{r}$ along the residue map of $\psi$, with $g_A'$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_A$ equal to $\rho^{+}.g_A$; maps $F_b : \rho.A_b.A \to \rho^{+}.A_b.A$ and $V_b : \rho^{+}.A_b.A \to \rho.A_b.A$ over the base, with $F_b$ followed by $g_A'$ equal to $\rho.g_A$ followed by $F$ and $V_b$ followed by $\rho.g_A$ equal to $g_A'$ followed by $V$; the degree shift $\rho^{+}.d = \rho.d + 1$; and the isogeny relations $u_b$ followed by $\rho^{+}.\varphi$ equals $\rho.\varphi$ followed by $F_b$, and $\rho^{+}.\varphi' = V_b$ followed by $\rho.\varphi'$ followed by $u_b$.
--
--   *The two transports.* Let $(X_1,\theta_1)$ be a formal module structure on $E$ via `coord`, $j_1 \le 1$ and $t_1 :$ `Rigidified r Φ B` with $t_1.X = X_1$, with $t_1$ a rigidification transport of $\rho$ with respect to $\theta_0, \kappa, \beta_0, \theta_1$ and parameter $j_1$, and with $t_1$ admissible for $\iota$ and $\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-j_1}$. Let $(X_2,\theta_2)$, $j_2 \le 1$ and $t_2$ be the analogous data for $\rho^{+}$, with $t_2$ admissible for $\iota$ and $(\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr})\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-j_2}$.
--
--   *The central translation.* Let $c \in \mathbb{Z}$ and let $Z \in GL_2(K_0)$ be the scalar unit given by $r \in K_0^{\times}$. The hypothesis `hact` is `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy ι Φ η Fr E₀` for the element $Z^{c}$ applied to the pair $\Xi B \psi (E,\rho)$ and $\Xi B (\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}) (E,\rho^{+})$: there exist an element $e$ of the centralizer of $\mathrm{range}(\Phi.\mathrm{actEnd}) \cup \{\Phi.\mathrm{varpiEnd}\}$ and natural numbers $k, m'$ with $E_0(e) = r^{k}\cdot (Z^{c})^{-1}$ in $M_2(K_0)$, with the power series of $e$ having kernel of degree $r^{2m'}$, and with the predicate `IsTranslate` holding for $\iota, \Phi, \eta, \mathrm{Fr}$, the series of $e$, $k$, $m'$ and the two points.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is the single equality of integers
--   $$t_2.n = t_1.n + 1 + c,$$
--   the natural numbers $t_1.n$ and $t_2.n$ (the exponents recorded by the rigidified objects $t_1$ and $t_2$) being taken in $\mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   This is the exponent bookkeeping of the Čerednik–Drinfeld dictionary: it records how the level exponent of an admissible Drinfeld transport changes when a rigidification of a fake elliptic curve is re-based along the Frobenius twist $\psi \mapsto \psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}$, the discrepancy being exactly $1$ plus the exponent $c$ of the central element $r^{c}$ by which the associated moduli points differ. It is used in the corresponding comparison of full level structures, [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.fullLevel_eq_of_isNormLevelTransport_of_isNormLevelTransport_frobTwist_one_of_isActBy`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.fullLevel_eq_of_isNormLevelTransport_of_isNormLevelTransport_frobTwist_one_of_isActBy).
